    "lawCode": "Amd §207, Pub Health L; add §209-I & Art 22 Part 2 §630-d, Tax L; add §97-llll,  St Fin L",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5902\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public health law, the tax law and the state\nfinance law, in relation to providing for taxpayer gifts for women's\ncancers education and prevention and establishing the women's cancers\neducation and prevention fund\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill establishes the women's cancers education and prevention\nfund, financed by optional contributions derived from a taxpayer\ncheck-off placed on all corporate and personal income tax forms.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends Subdivision 1 of section 207 of the public health law\nadding a new paragraph (1) to add women's cancers to the health care\nand wellness education and outreach program within the Department of\nHealth.\n\nSection 2 and 3 adds new sections, 209-I and 630-d, respectively; to\nthe tax law to allow corporate and individual taxpayers the option to\ncontribute to the women's cancers education and prevention program\nthrough a tax check-off on the tax return.\n\nSection 4 adds a new section, 97-1111, to the state finance law, to\nestablish the women's cancers education and prevention fund under the,\njoint custody of the commissioner of taxation and finance and the\nstate comptroller.\n\nSection 5 sets forth the effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nWomen cancers, defined in this bill to include cervical, endometrial,\ngestational trophoblastic tumor, ovarian, uterine sarcoma, vaginal,\nand vulvae, claim thousands of lives each year. While much education\nhas effectively focused on cancers such as breast cancer, it is\nimportant to provide for additional avenues for New Yorkers to raise\nfunds for women's cancers education and prevention programs by having\na voluntarily taxpayer check-off on both individual and corporate\ntaxpayer tax forms. These funds will be used to educate the public\nregarding the existences of women cancers, screening options, and tips\nfor a healthy lifestyle.\n\nThrough education and awareness, lives can be saved, particularly if\nwomen understand the need for screenings and preventative measures\nthat may be taken to reduce the risks for cancers.\n\nRaising funds for this purpose will help to ensure that more women are\nreached with this vital information.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2014. S5871A- reported to Finance, A5689B - passed Assembly\n\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nImmediately\n\n",
